# Privacy Policy for Calo

**Developer:** mosaappsmarket
**Effective Date:** August 21, 2026

mosaappsmarket ("we", "us", or "our") operates the **Calo** mobile application (the "App"). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and protect your information when you use Calo, and describes your rights regarding that information.

## Information We Collect

When you use Calo, we collect the following information:

- **Account Information:** When you sign in using Google Authentication, we receive and store your Google User ID to identify your account within our systems.
- **Food Analysis Data:** When you upload or capture a photo of food for analysis, we process the image and store the resulting nutritional information — including calories, fat, protein, and carbohydrates — in our database. This data is linked to your User ID so that your history and progress can be saved and displayed to you within the App.

We do not collect your name, email address, or profile photo directly, though these may be accessible to us through the Google Authentication process depending on the permissions you grant.

## How We Use Your Information

We use the information described above to:

- Authenticate and identify your account
- Save and display your food analysis history within the App
- Provide personalized nutritional tracking features
- Maintain and improve the functionality of the App

We do not sell your personal information to third parties, and we do not use your data for advertising purposes.

## Data Retention

We retain your User ID and food analysis data for as long as your account remains active. We do not automatically delete this data. Your data is only deleted when you submit a deletion request as described in the "Data Deletion" section below.

## Data Deletion

You can request the deletion of your account and all associated data (including your User ID and food analysis history) at any time by sending an email to:

**alimosaalimosa@gmail.com**

Please include your account details (such as the email address associated with your Google Sign-In) in your request so we can locate and delete your data. We will process deletion requests within a reasonable timeframe and confirm once your data has been permanently removed from our database.

## Third-Party Services

Calo uses **Google Sign-In** for authentication. When you sign in, Google may collect information according to its own privacy policy. We encourage you to review [Google's Privacy Policy](https://policies.google.com/privacy) for more information on how Google handles your data.

We do not share your food analysis data or User ID with any other third party.

## Security

We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your personal information from unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

## Children's Privacy

Calo is not intended for use by children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can delete it.

## Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with a revised effective date. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.

## Contact Us

If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or how your data is handled, please contact us at:

